## Hints for Future Agents
Do not omit false when serializing RawKvEvent: normalized raw events lose their original unknown extra keys, so omission can turn a negative decision into positive on decode. Normalized RouterEvent and PlacementEvent may omit false because their absence means false. Non-UTF-8 binary extra keys must stay rejected as on main; accepted UTF-8 binary keys retain existing GPU hash/namespace normalization but cannot establish shared-cache eligibility. Do not add eligibility back to KvCacheStoreData.

## Codebase Discoveries
The derived positional RawKvEvent serializer skips optional fields and does not match the vLLM positional decoder layout. Test batches therefore preserve the outer tuple and encode events as named maps. The enum field requires fixture updates across router, consolidator, and LLM tests. This atomic decoder slice is 517 changed lines; separating fixture updates would leave a non-compiling part.

